  "body": "Offering an impressive 148m² of single-level living, this is one of Kensington Park's most spacious apartments, combining the proportions of a home with the ease of apartment living.\r\n\r\nNortheast facing and wonderfully light, 73 Parkside Drive enjoys a peaceful outlook across the native treetops of Alice Eaves Scenic Reserve. Inside, house like proportions are immediately apparent, with expansive open plan living, oversized bedrooms, wide hallways and exceptional storage throughout.\r\n\r\nA particularly versatile feature is the rare third room, providing the flexibility to create a media room, home office, library or hobby space. An increasingly sought after addition that is seldom found in apartment living.\r\n\r\nElevator access provides effortless access from the two secure basement car parks (and generous storage locker) directly to the lobby and your second-floor home, adding another layer of everyday convenience.\r\n\r\nLife at Kensington Park is about enjoying more and maintaining less. Residents have exclusive access to an impressive array of resort-style amenities, including a heated indoor pool, gym, sauna, pétanque court, putting green and acres of beautifully landscaped grounds. The on-site garden café provides a relaxed setting for coffee, brunch and time with friends, while Orewa Beach is just a short stroll away from Kensington Park's iconic clocktower entrance.\r\n\r\nFreehold unit title ownership, supported by an established body corporate, offers the security of home ownership with the freedom of a low-maintenance lifestyle, ideal for avid travellers, busy professionals or anyone ready to enjoy a more effortless way of living.\r\n\r\nThis is downsizing without compromise, exceptional space, beautiful surroundings and the convenience of a truly lock up and leave lifestyle.\r\n\r\nVisit our weekend open home or call today to arrange for a private viewing.\r\n\r\nTo view the property documents copy this link into your browser: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/CBVA",
